{
  "about": "Butler's Lives for nine of January's saints, published on the owner's word of 2026-11-11 (call 34, \"yes Butler January\"; no priest's check), word for word with any passage of Roman doctrine against the Orthodox Church cut and shown: the London stereotype edition (John Murphy), vol. I for the January saints and vol. II for St Polyeuctus, whom Butler keeps on February 13. The first scan of each volume is Princeton Theological Seminary's (its page images are read); the second, the Digital Library of India's, is a copy of the same stereotype plates, line for line the same. The others are the same text set again at Edinburgh (1798) and Derby (1842).",
